1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,013
A revenue manager told me a custom question costs her half a day of
pivot tables.

2
00:00:08,863 --> 00:00:10,890
So I built this: she just asks.

3
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:15,132
It's a simulated hotel group, and all the data's made up.

4
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:18,971
Which room type at Mountain Lodge earned the most this year?

5
00:00:19,821 --> 00:00:21,741
It writes one SQL query,

6
00:00:22,591 --> 00:00:25,151
and before anything runs, a guard checks it.

7
00:00:26,001 --> 00:00:29,713
Here's the guard's verdict: read-only, and only these tables.

8
00:00:30,328 --> 00:00:32,269
And here's where the answer came from.

9
00:00:33,119 --> 00:00:37,151
The tables it read, and the revenue definition the hotel agreed on.

10
00:00:38,001 --> 00:00:39,879
It didn't guess what revenue means.

11
00:00:40,729 --> 00:00:41,753
It looked it up.

12
00:00:42,603 --> 00:00:44,651
And the SQL's right there to check.

13
00:00:45,266 --> 00:00:46,354
Now a follow-up.

14
00:00:47,204 --> 00:00:48,548
And at Beach Resort?

15
00:00:49,398 --> 00:00:52,598
It works out I mean the same question for the other property,

16
00:00:53,448 --> 00:00:55,603
shows me how it read it, and answers.

17
00:00:56,219 --> 00:00:59,846
If I ask for guest phone numbers as an analyst, it says no,

18
00:01:00,696 --> 00:01:04,109
and even if the model slipped, the guard would stop the query.

19
00:01:04,719 --> 00:01:08,218
Every morning a check runs five rules with no model at all.

20
00:01:09,068 --> 00:01:13,313
Here it caught a suite priced at fifty dollars instead of about five
hundred.

21
00:01:13,922 --> 00:01:17,271
On my test questions it gets ninety-nine percent right,

22
00:01:18,121 --> 00:01:19,593
and every held-out one,

23
00:01:20,443 --> 00:01:23,046
for about twenty-eight cents per thousand questions.

24
00:01:23,641 --> 00:01:25,390
It's live, with no sign-in.

25
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:28,246
The link's below, and so is the code.
